        "selected_case": "Exec/DoublyPeriodic",
        "selected_solver": "REMORA",
        "modifications": [],
        "reasoning": "The case is set up to study the BOMEX (Barbados Oceanic and Meteorological Experiment) case using the ERF model. Domain and resolution are specified to capture the dynamics of the BOMEX case. Initial conditions for theta_l and q_t are taken from Siebesma 2003 to ensure consistency with previous studies. BOMEX forcings are prescribed to drive the simulation. Deardorff TKE SGS and Kessler microphysics are used to represent subgrid-scale processes and cloud microphysics. Periodic lateral BCs are applied to allow for continuous flow through the domain. A top sponge layer is included to prevent wave reflection at the top of the domain. A 3-hour spin-up is performed to allow the model to adjust to the initial conditions and forcings. Hourly averages are collected for the final 3 hours to provide a statistically robust dataset for analysis. Baseline weights: configuration_complexity=0.100, development_activity=0.100, domain_models=0.100, grid_specifications=0.200, path_hierarchy=0.150, physics_parameters=0.300, resource_requirements=0.050.",
